r chart if you  saw 74 did not have to go on to our  molecular testing at 150 for a price  test  kit that we use or price per test i  should say  so you can see the savings that we had  just over a three month period  so lastly i'm just going to get into a  few case studies just to show you  how this has impacted us here  at leahy  so the first case study we had a blood  culture flag positive  the gram stain result  was gram-negative rods  we did a sepsi typer and we ended up  with b frag well as you know b frag is  an anaerobe  when we reported this we reported it out  as gram-negative rods now we can't say  that it's an anaerobic or negative rod  because at this point we do not know  so with gram-negative rods  then we were able to perform the sepsi  typer it gave us the b frog's result  which we were then able to update  and we were able to update it in the  computer in the patient's chart  and therefore id pharmacy was then able  to  change  the antibiotic therapy  to  an appropriate  antibiotic for this particular organism  so again typically gram-negative rod  they're going to choose one set  of their they're going to choose one  type of therapy for a gram negative rod  and as you can imagine if it's an  anaerobe they need to choose a different  one so this was great for them to see  definitely helped provide in patient  care  the next case study was positive blood  culture flagged and this one  was gram-positive cocci in clusters and  it was suggestive of stuff  so this is how we report it if we see  gram-positive cocci and clusters we  always say suggesting stuff if that's  what it looks like to us  again performed the sepsi typer  and  came out with aerococcus urane so  you can imagine how surprised we were  when this result came out we're thinking  it's going to come off as a staphorious  or cognitive staff so to see that it was  an aerococcus that really blew a lot of  our text minds we were just like oh my  god this is just amazing  and aerocaucus is one